            <ArticleTitle>Superiorly based facial artery musculomucosal flap: A versatile pedicled flap.</ArticleTitle>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1002/hed.24997</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="BACKGROUND" NlmCategory="BACKGROUND">The superiorly based facial artery musculomucosal (FAMM) flap is pedicled on the angular artery. This flap offers a well-vascularized mucosal surface allowing closure of medium size defects, most frequently within the oral cavity and intranasal region.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="METHODS" NlmCategory="METHODS">We describe a superiorly based harvest of the FAMM flap, which may be used for closure of multiple head and neck surgical defects. An operative technique video is provided, which can be viewed online.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="RESULTS" NlmCategory="RESULTS">Our results demonstrate a fast and relatively straightforward harvest technique of the FAMM flap. This intraoral flap is a useful reconstructive tool, which also has the advantage to leave no visible external scars.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSION" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">The superiorly pedicled FAMM flap is a versatile and effective technique that may be integrated in the algorithm for reconstruction of head and neck defects.</AbstractText>
                <CopyrightInformation>© 2017 Wiley Periodicals, Inc.</CopyrightInformation>
            </Abstract>
